8.1. General rules

8.1.1. Within the scope of this Offer, the Company, Partner and Client must comply with the current legislation, this Offer and the provisions specified in the "SAFAAR" system in exercising their rights and fulfilling their obligations.

8.2. Rights and obligations of the company

8.2.1. Obligations of the company:

providing system service through the "SAFAAR" system in accordance with the terms of this Offer;

try to ensure the stable operation of the system within the limits of technical capabilities;

Processing users' personal data in accordance with the Privacy Policy and applicable legislation;

take necessary measures to eliminate technical failures or interruptions when they are detected.

8.2.2. Rights of the company:

change the interface, functional capabilities, tariffs and special conditions of service in order to improve the service, security and optimization;

Temporarily limit or stop access to the system in case of gross violation of the Offer, Privacy Policy, legal requirements or ethical standards by the user;

temporarily closing, upgrading or limiting functionality of individual sections of the system due to technical, organizational or legal requirements.

8.2.3. The Company is not the owner or operator of the residential or recreational facility and is not directly responsible for the service (condition of the facility, compliance with images, security) and is not directly responsible for this service. The service is provided by the directly responsible Partner.

8.3. Rights and obligations of the partner

8.3.1. Obligations of the partner:

provide correct and up-to-date information about the object (address, picture, price, available spaces, amenities);

provide the booked object to the Client in the agreed time and conditions;

to be fully responsible for the facility's safety, sanitation and compliance with other legal requirements;

Correctly and clearly display the terms of service, price and cancellation policy in the "SAFAAR" application, update them in a timely manner in case of changes;

Reviewing customer complaints and claims within the scope of their authority, cooperating with competent authorities when necessary.

8.3.2. Partner's rights:

Independent determination of the price of one's object, the number of available places and reservation conditions in the "SAFAAR" application;

choose a payment and cancellation policy that is convenient for him;

stop using the system service in compliance with this Offer and legal requirements.

8.3.3. The Partner is obliged to pay the fee (commission) for the system service in accordance with the rules of this Offer and make mutual settlements with the Company in a timely manner.

8.4. Customer's Rights and Responsibilities

8.4.1. Customer rights:

Reservation of accommodation and recreation services through the "SAFAAR" system, monitoring of the reservation status and use of other possibilities of the system;

Require complete and reliable information about the offered object from the partner;

Voluntarily connect or opt out of the SMS subscription service;

to submit appeals, complaints and suggestions in the manner provided by this Offer and legislation.

8.4.2. Customer Obligations:

provide correct and up-to-date information during registration and booking;

complying with the rules of the internal procedure established in the object, paying the service fee on time by the chosen method;

not to violate legal requirements, ethical norms and the terms of this Offer when using the system.

9.1. General rules of liability

9.1.1. The parties are liable for violations of the terms of this Offer in accordance with applicable law and this Offer.

9.1.2. The Company may generally be liable only for actual damages (actual losses) caused by improper performance of its system service obligations. The company assumes no responsibility for lost profits.

9.2. Responsibility for the condition of the object and the quality of service

9.2.1. The Partner shall be fully and independently responsible for:

the accuracy of the information and pictures provided about the object;

compliance of the facility with safety, sanitary and hygiene and other legal requirements;

provision of the booked service in the agreed period and conditions;

availability of necessary permits and licenses for operation (if required).

9.2.2. Company:

does not take any responsibility for the actual condition, quality and safety of the object;

It is not responsible for obligations related to the residential relationship between the Partner and the Client;

It is not responsible for any damages related to improper provision of the service by the partner.

Such relationships are resolved directly within the framework of the relationship between the Client and the Partner.

9.2.3. When there are claims regarding the quality of service, the Client has the right to first send a claim to the Partner, as well as to apply to the relevant state control bodies in accordance with the procedure established by law.

9.3. System interruptions and technical limitations

9.3.1. The company tries to ensure stable operation of the SAFAAR system, but cannot guarantee continuous operation in the following cases:

failures in internet providers, communication operators or hosting providers;

server and equipment technical failures;

DDoS-attacks, cyber-attacks and other threats to information security;

emergency technical work.

9.3.2. In such cases, the Company will try to take measures to restore the system, but is not responsible for direct or indirect lost profits, data loss, service delays, or other consequences unless the damage was caused by the Company's willful or gross negligence.

9.4. Force majeure

9.4.1. The parties are released from liability for failure to fully or partially fulfill obligations in the event of force majeure, including:

natural disasters (earthquake, flood, landslide, storm, heavy snowfall, etc.);

war, hostilities, terrorism, public unrest;

epidemic, pandemic, quarantine restrictions;

decisions of state bodies, local authorities and other authorized organizations that lead to restriction or prohibition of the service;

major accidents in communication, power supply and transport infrastructure and other similar situations.

9.4.2. The Party affected by the Force Majeure shall notify the other Party(ies) as soon as possible and shall take measures to mitigate the consequences.
